(   \(30-55 years\), and broad toward older cohorts.) Tj
T*
(   * Demographic Characteristics: Low and falling birth rates \(TFR < 1.6\), low mortality, high) Tj
T*
(   life expectancy. Proportion of children is smaller than the reproductive adult cohort.) Tj
T*
(   * Typical Nations: Japan, Italy, South Korea, Germany.) Tj
T*
(   * Socio-Economic Challenges: Rapid population aging \(graying society\), escalating geriatric) Tj
T*
(   healthcare and pension expenditures, severe industrial labor shortages, and shrinking consumer) Tj
T*
(   tax bases.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Stationary / Stable Population Pyramid \(Rectangular / Bell Shape\):) Tj
T*
(   * Geometric Profile: Uniform, near-vertical sides with approximately equal widths across all) Tj
T*
(   age cohorts from infancy through middle age, tapering gently only at advanced ages \(75+ years\).) Tj
T*
(   * Demographic Characteristics: Low birth and death rates with TFR hovering near replacement) Tj
T*
(   level \(2.1\). Zero or near-zero population growth.) Tj
T*
(   * Typical Nations: Sweden, France, Norway, United States.) Tj
T*
(   * Socio-Economic Stability: Balanced dependency ratios, predictable educational and labor) Tj
T*
(   requirements, and manageable social security burdens.) Tj
T*
