(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the Epidemiological Triad \(Agent, Host, Environment\), and explain the Environmental Determinants of human health and health equity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Epidemiological Triad and Environmental Determinants of Human Health:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Epidemiological Triad Model:) Tj
T*
(   The foundational paradigm of environmental epidemiology, conceptualizing disease causality as) Tj
T*
(   an interactive balance between three interdependent components:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. The Agent: The biological pathogen \(bacterium, virus, protozoan\), physical factor) Tj
T*
(   \(ionizing radiation, acoustic noise, thermal heat\), or toxic chemical \(lead, arsenic, benzene\)) Tj
T*
(   whose presence, excessive presence, or deficiency is the immediate cause of disease.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. The Host: The human being who harbors the disease. Host susceptibility is modulated by) Tj
T*
(   intrinsic biological factors: genetic polymorphisms, immunological immunocompetence,) Tj
T*
(   nutritional status, age, sex, and underlying chronic comorbidities.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. The Environment: The external physical, chemical, biological, and socio-economic matrix) Tj
T*
(   that facilitates transmission of the agent from reservoirs to the susceptible host:) Tj
T*
(   * Physical Environment: Ambient temperature, humidity, rainfall \(governing vector breeding\),) Tj
T*
(   altitude.) Tj
T*
(   * Chemical Environment: Water purity, atmospheric particulate levels, pesticide residues in) Tj
T*
(   food.) Tj
T*
(   * Biological Environment: Reservoir animal populations, insect vectors, sanitation) Tj
T*
(   infrastructure.) Tj
T*
(   * Socio-Economic Environment: Housing density, poverty, piped drinking water access,) Tj
T*
(   occupational protective regulations.) Tj
T*
(   2. WHO Framework of Environmental Determinants of Health:) Tj
T*
(   According to the World Health Organization \(WHO\), nearly 24% of all global human deaths \(and) Tj
T*
(   28% of deaths in children under five\) are directly attributable to modifiable environmental) Tj
T*
(   risks:) Tj
T*
(   - Ambient and Household Air Pollution: Responsible for ~7 million premature deaths annually) Tj
T*
(   \(ischemic heart disease, stroke, lung cancer, childhood pneumonia\).) Tj
T*
(   - Unsafe Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene \(WASH\): Drives diarrheal diseases \(cholera, typhoid,) Tj
T*
(   rotavirus\).) Tj
T*
(   - Toxic Chemical Exposures: Lead poisoning contributing to intellectual disability;) Tj
T*
(   agrochemicals causing chronic kidney disease.) Tj
T*
(   3. Health Equity and the Environmental Justice Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   Environmental health burdens are NOT distributed equitably across human populations.) Tj
T*
(   Marginalized communities, racial minorities, and informal urban slum dwellers reside) Tj
T*
ET

