(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the transmission cycles and climate sensitivity of Vector-Borne Diseases in tropical agroecosystems: Dengue and Malaria.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Vector-Borne Epidemiology, Pathogen Life Cycles, and Climate Sensitivity: Dengue and Malaria:) Tj
T*
(   1. Malaria \(Plasmodium spp. / Anopheles Vector\):) Tj
T*
(   - Pathogen: Apicomplexan protozoan parasites \(Plasmodium falciparum - lethal malignant tertian) Tj
T*
(   malaria; P. vivax - relapsing benign tertian malaria\).) Tj
T*
(   - Biological Vector: Female Anopheles mosquitoes \(e.g., Anopheles culicifacies, A. stephensi\),) Tj
T*
(   which require protein-rich blood meals for ovarian egg development.) Tj
T*
(   - Transmission Cycle \(Sporogonic vs Schizogonic Stages\):) Tj
T*
(   * Sporozoites injected during mosquito bite travel within 30 minutes to liver hepatocytes) Tj
T*
(   \(Exo-erythrocytic schizogony\).) Tj
T*
(   * Merozoites erupt into the bloodstream, invading erythrocytes \(Erythrocytic schizogony\),) Tj
T*
(   feeding on hemoglobin, and forming hemozoin pigment.) Tj
T*
(   * Synchronous erythrocyte rupture releases merozoites, pyrogenic cytokines \(TNF-alpha, IL-1\),) Tj
T*
(   and hemozoin, triggering classic paroxysms of shaking chills, spiking fevers \(40-41 deg C\), and) Tj
T*
(   profuse sweating.) Tj
T*
(   * P. vivax forms dormant liver stages \(hypnozoites\) that cause clinical relapses months to) Tj
T*
(   years later.) Tj
T*
(   2. Dengue Fever \(Dengue Virus / Aedes aegypti Vector\):) Tj
T*
(   - Pathogen: Flavivirus with four distinct antigenically related serotypes \(DENV-1, DENV-2,) Tj
T*
(   DENV-3, DENV-4\).) Tj
T*
(   - Biological Vector: Aedes aegypti and Aedes albopictus \(day-biting, peridomestic mosquitoes) Tj
T*
(   breeding in artificial freshwater collections: flower pots, discarded tires, plastic) Tj
T*
(   containers, overhead water tanks\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pathophysiological Complications:) Tj
T*
(   * Primary Infection: Self-limiting 'break-bone fever' \(severe retro-orbital headache,) Tj
T*
(   arthralgia, myalgia, maculopapular rash\). Induces lifelong homologous immunity to that specific) Tj
T*
(   serotype.) Tj
T*
(   * Secondary Heterologous Infection & Antibody-Dependent Enhancement \(ADE\):) Tj
T*
(   * If an individual previously infected with DENV-1 is later infected with DENV-2,) Tj
T*
(   non-neutralizing cross-reactive antibodies bind the new virus. Rather than neutralizing it, the) Tj
T*
(   antibody-virus complex binds to Fc-gamma receptors on monocytes, accelerating viral uptake) Tj
T*
(   100-fold!) Tj
T*
(   * Triggers a massive cytokine storm, vascular endothelial permeability hyper-activation, and) Tj
T*
(   thrombocytopenia, culminating in Dengue Hemorrhagic Fever \(DHF\) and fatal circulatory Dengue) Tj
T*
(   Shock Syndrome \(DSS\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Climate Sensitivity and Global Warming Acceleration:) Tj
T*
(   - Extrinsic Incubation Period \(EIP\): The time required for a pathogen to replicate inside the) Tj
T*
(   mosquito gut and migrate to the salivary glands. For P. falciparum, warming ambient) Tj
T*
(   temperatures from 20 deg C to 28 deg C slashes the EIP from 30 days down to only 10 days!) Tj
T*
(   Because mosquito survival beyond 30 days is low, temperature elevation exponentially increases) Tj
T*
(   the proportion of infectious mosquitoes.) Tj
T*
(   - Expansion of Spatial Altitudinal Range: Warmer winters and shifts in monsoonal precipitation) Tj
T*
(   allow Aedes and Anopheles vectors to invade highland montane cities previously protected by) Tj
T*
(   cool temperatures \(e.g., Nairobi, Ethiopian highlands, Himalayan foothills\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
