(   1. Definition of Endocrine Disruptors \(US EPA\):) Tj
T*
(   Exogenous chemical substances or mixtures that alter one or more functions of the endocrine) Tj
T*
(   system and consequently cause adverse health effects in an intact organism, its progeny, or) Tj
T*
(   populations.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Monotonic Dose-Response Curves \(NMDRCs\):) Tj
T*
(   Unlike classical industrial poisons where toxicity follows Paracelsus' linear dogma \('the dose) Tj
T*
(   makes the poison'\), EDCs frequently exhibit U-shaped or inverted U-shaped dose-response curves,) Tj
T*
(   exerting potent physiological and epigenetic disruptions at ultra-low nanomolar concentrations) Tj
T*
(   \(parts-per-billion or parts-per-trillion\) while displaying minimal toxicity at high doses!) Tj
T*
(   2. Bisphenol A \(BPA\): Molecular Mimicry and Cellular Mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Identity: 2,2-bis\(4-hydroxyphenyl\)propane. Widely synthesized as a monomer in the) Tj
T*
(   production of polycarbonate plastics \(baby bottles, food containers\) and epoxy resin coatings) Tj
T*
(   lining metal food and beverage cans.) Tj
T*
(   - Xeno-Estrogenic Activity:) Tj
T*
(   * BPA contains two phenolic rings structurally analogous to the natural female steroid hormone) Tj
T*
(   17-beta-estradiol \(E2\).) Tj
T*
(   * It binds to nuclear Estrogen Receptors alpha and beta \(ER-alpha and ER-beta\) and) Tj
T*
(   membrane-bound G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1 \(GPER1\), inducing allosteric dimerization) Tj
T*
(   and recruiting co-activator proteins that trigger premature estrogen-responsive gene) Tj
T*
(   transcription.) Tj
T*
(   * Developmental & Reproductive Pathologies: Early fetal exposure induces altered prostate gland) Tj
T*
(   morphogenesis, premature puberty in females, reduced sperm counts in males, polycystic ovarian) Tj
T*
(   syndrome \(PCOS\), and elevated lifetime risk of hormone-dependent breast and prostate cancers.) Tj
T*
(   3. Phthalate Esters: Anti-Androgenic and Metabolic Disruption:) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Identity: Dialkyl or alkyl aryl esters of 1,2-benzenedicarboxylic acid [e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Di\(2-ethylhexyl\) phthalate, DEHP; Di-n-butyl phthalate, DBP]. Used as plasticizers to confer) Tj
T*
(   flexibility to rigid polyvinyl chloride \(PVC\) plastics.) Tj
T*
(   - Anti-Androgenic Endocrine Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Phthalates are not chemically bound to the PVC polymer matrix; they leach continuously into) Tj
T*
(   food, milk, and medical IV tubing.) Tj
T*
(   * In fetal male Leydig cells during the critical developmental 'masculinization programming) Tj
T*
(   window,' phthalate metabolites down-regulate the expression of the steroidogenic acute) Tj
T*
(   regulatory \(StAR\) protein and cytochrome P450 side-chain cleavage enzyme \(CYP11A1\), shutting) Tj
T*
(   down fetal testosterone biosynthesis.) Tj
T*
(   * Phthalate Syndrome: Induces congenital urogenital abnormalities: Cryptorchidism \(undescended) Tj
T*
(   testes\), Hypospadias \(abnormal urethral opening\), shortened Anogenital Distance \(AGD\), and) Tj
T*
(   adult testicular dysgenesis syndrome.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
