(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the pathophysiology of Occupational Pulmonary Fibrosis, analyzing alveolar macrophage activation in Silicosis and Asbestosis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Occupational Pulmonary Diseases: Alveolar Macrophage Pathology in Silicosis and Asbestosis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Deposition Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   Inhaled atmospheric particulates are deposited in the respiratory tract based on aerodynamic) Tj
T*
(   diameter:) Tj
T*
(   - Particles > 10 micrometers are captured by nasal hairs and nasopharyngeal mucus.) Tj
T*
(   - Particles between 2.5 and 10 micrometers settle in the tracheobronchial tree and are) Tj
T*
(   eliminated by the mucociliary escalator.) Tj
T*
(   - Respirable Particulates \(< 2.5 to 5.0 micrometers, PM2.5\): Evade mechanical mucociliary) Tj
T*
(   defenses and penetrate deep into terminal respiratory bronchioles and un-ciliated alveoli.) Tj
T*
(   2. Molecular Pathogenesis of Silicosis:) Tj
T*
(   - Etiology: Inhalation of respirable crystalline silicon dioxide \(alpha-quartz\) dust generated) Tj
T*
