(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the drivers of Zoonotic Disease Emergence and viral spillover, and formulate the collaborative architecture of the One Health approach.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Zoonotic Spillover Dynamics, Planetary Health Drivers, and the One Health Framework:) Tj
T*
(   1. Zoonoses and Interspecies Viral Spillover:) Tj
T*
(   Over 75% of all newly emerging infectious diseases \(EIDs\) affecting humans \(e.g., SARS-CoV-1,) Tj
T*
(   MERS-CoV, SARS-CoV-2, Ebola, Marburg, H5N1 Avian Influenza, Nipah virus, HIV\) are zoonotic,) Tj
T*
(   originating in wildlife reservoir populations \(bats, rodents, wild birds, non-human primates\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Anthropogenic Planetary Drivers of Spillover:) Tj
T*
(   Spillover does not occur because wildlife species are aggressive; it occurs because industrial) Tj
T*
(   human activities aggressively disrupt natural ecological boundary barriers:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Tropical Deforestation and Habitat Fragmentation:) Tj
T*
(   Clearing primary rainforests for commercial cattle ranching, oil palm monocultures, and logging) Tj
T*
(   forces displaced wild animals \(e.g., fruit bats of family Pteropodidae\) to forage in peri-urban) Tj
T*
(   fruit orchards, livestock farms, and human habitations, exponentially elevating wildlife-human) Tj
T*
(   contact rates.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Intensive Livestock Industrialization:) Tj
T*
(   High-density monoculture livestock feedlots \(millions of genetically uniform pigs, poultry\)) Tj
T*
(   situated adjacent to fragmented forest edges act as 'amplifying hosts.' Low genetic diversity) Tj
T*
(   and immunosuppressive housing conditions allow wild viruses to mutate and amplify rapidly) Tj
T*
