T*
(   - 3. Commercial Wildlife Trade and Wet Markets:) Tj
T*
(   Crowding diverse wild species \(bats, civets, pangolins\) together under stressful, unhygienic) Tj
T*
(   conditions in commercial wet markets facilitates inter-species viral recombination and) Tj
T*
(   high-volume human aerosol exposure.) Tj
T*
(   3. The 'One Health' Integrated Transdisciplinary Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   Endorsed by the Quadripartite Alliance \(WHO, WOAH, FAO, and UNEP\), One Health asserts that) Tj
T*
(   human medicine CANNOT function in isolation from veterinary medicine and environmental) Tj
T*
(   conservation:) Tj
T*
(   - Core Pillars of Action:) Tj
T*
(   * 1. Upstream Ecological Surveillance: Monitoring viral diversity \(virome discovery\) in natural) Tj
T*
(   wildlife reservoir populations before spillover occurs.) Tj
T*
(   * 2. Integrated Biosecurity at the Animal-Human Interface: Enforcing strict biosecurity) Tj
T*
(   barriers on livestock farms, ending illegal bushmeat trafficking, and closing commercial) Tj
T*
(   wildlife wet markets.) Tj
T*
(   * 3. Joint Multi-Sectoral Outbreak Response: Unifying public health departments, veterinary) Tj
T*
(   epidemiologists, and forestry wildlife rangers under centralized command structures to detect) Tj
T*
(   and contain novel pathogen outbreaks at the source.) Tj
