(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the history, grassroots leadership, and policy impacts of the Chipko Movement \(1973\), evaluating its eco-feminist dimensions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Chipko Movement \(1973\): Grassroots Eco-Feminism, Gandhian Satyagraha, and Forest Policy) Tj
T*
(   Reform:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Context and Commercial Exploitation:) Tj
T*
(   Following the 1962 Sino-Indian War, extensive military border road construction in the Garhwal) Tj
T*
(   Himalayas \(Uttarakhand\) triggered aggressive commercial timber felling by the state Forest) Tj
T*
(   Department, auctioning pristine oak and ash forests to private commercial manufacturing) Tj
T*
(   corporations \(including the Symonds sporting goods company\).) Tj
T*
(   - Ecological Disaster: Deforestation destroyed root anchoring networks on steep Himalayan) Tj
T*
(   slopes, culminating in the catastrophic July 1970 Alaknanda River flash floods, which submerged) Tj
T*
(   over 100 km2 of land, washed away six major bridges, and destroyed hundreds of villages.) Tj
T*
(   2. Grassroots Genesis and the Philosophy of Chipko:) Tj
T*
(   - Formed under the leadership of Chandi Prasad Bhatt and the Dasholi Gram Swarajya Mandal) Tj
T*
(   \(DGSM\), local villagers realized that their survival was inextricably linked to forest) Tj
T*
(   stability.) Tj
T*
(   - Gandhian Non-Violent Direct Action \(Satyagraha\): When commercial loggers arrived, villagers) Tj
T*
(   resolved to physically hug the marked trees \(in Hindi, 'Chipko' = 'to cling' or 'to embrace'\),) Tj
T*
(   putting their own bodies between the axemen and the trees.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Epic Stand at Reni Village \(March 1974\) and Eco-Feminism:) Tj
T*
(   - The state administration and loggers used a subterfuge to lure all local men away to Chamoli) Tj
T*
(   town to collect compensation.) Tj
T*
(   - Seeing commercial logging trucks arrive in the village, Gaura Devi, a 50-year-old illiterate) Tj
T*
(   Bhotiya tribal widow, organized 27 village women.) Tj
T*
(   - Facing armed loggers, the women formed human chains around the ash trees, declaring: 'The) Tj
T*
(   forest is our mother's home; we will not let you cut it down.' The loggers retreated, and the) Tj
T*
(   government appointed the Virendra Kumar Committee, which formally confirmed the ecological) Tj
T*
(   fragility of the catchment.) Tj
T*
(   4. Sunderlal Bahuguna and Global Eco-Centric Philosophy:) Tj
T*
(   - Bahuguna undertook an epic 4,800-kilometer foot march \(padyatra\) along the Himalayan spine) Tj
T*
(   from Kashmir to Kohima, raising international awareness.) Tj
T*
ET

