T*
(   2. The Hydroelectric Threat:) Tj
T*
(   In 1973, the Kerala State Electricity Board \(KSEB\) proposed the construction of a) Tj
T*
(   131-meter-high concrete gravity dam across the pristine Kunthipuzha River, submerging 830) Tj
T*
(   hectares of primary tropical rainforest to generate 120 MW of peak hydroelectric power.) Tj
T*
(   3. Science Activism by Kerala Sasthra Sahithya Parishad \(KSSP\):) Tj
T*
(   - KSSP \(Kerala Science Literature Movement\), a voluntary mass organization of school teachers,) Tj
T*
(   university scientists, and writers, transformed the campaign from an emotional protest into a) Tj
T*
(   rigorous, scientifically grounded environmental battle.) Tj
T*
(   - Interdisciplinary Technoeconomic Survey:) Tj
T*
(   KSSP scientists published an exhaustive alternative assessment proving that:) Tj
T*
(   * The dam would destroy rare, irreplaceable endemic biodiversity and primitive floral) Tj
T*
(   germplasm.) Tj
T*
(   * The actual electricity generated \(120 MW\) would contribute < 10% to Kerala's grid and could) Tj
T*
(   be achieved far more cheaply by reducing transmission and distribution \(T&D\) losses and) Tj
T*
(   upgrading existing thermal plants.) Tj
T*
(   * The promised irrigation benefits were marginal compared to the permanent destruction of the) Tj
T*
(   microclimate.) Tj
T*
(   4. Creative Public Communication Campaigns:) Tj
T*
(   - KSSP mobilized mass public awareness through street plays, traveling song processions) Tj
T*
(   \(jathas\), newspaper columns, and environmental poetry \(led by renowned poet Sugathakumari\).) Tj
T*
(   - Prominent national scientists \(Dr. Salim Ali, Satish Dhawan, M.S. Swaminathan\) submitted) Tj
T*
(   expert reports to the Central Government urging total preservation.) Tj
T*
(   5. National Policy Triumph \(1985\):) Tj
T*
(   - In 1983, Prime Minister Indira Gandhi formally declared that the Silent Valley hydroelectric) Tj
T*
(   project was cancelled to protect the ecosystem.) Tj
T*
(   - In November 1985, Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi officially inaugurated the Silent Valley) Tj
T*
(   National Park, and the valley subsequently became the core protected zone of the Nilgiri) Tj
T*
(   Biosphere Reserve.) Tj
