(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the environmental ethos of the Bishnoi Community, the 29 Principles of Guru Jambheshwar, and the 1730 Khejarli martyrdom.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Bishnoi Environmental Ethic, Guru Jambheshwar's Principles, and the Khejarli Sacrifice:) Tj
T*
(   1. Spiritual Foundation and Guru Jambheshwar \(1485 AD\):) Tj
T*
(   Following a devastating 12-year drought in the Thar Desert of Rajasthan, Guru Jambheshwar) Tj
T*
(   \(Jambhoji\) founded the Bishnoi community in 1485. He recognized that ecological degradation,) Tj
T*
(   deforestation, and indiscriminate animal slaughter had intensified drought vulnerability.) Tj
T*
(   - The 29 Principles \(Bish = 20, Noi = 9\):) Tj
T*
(   Codified 29 mandatory socio-ecological commandments governing Bishnoi life, prominently) Tj
T*
(   including:) Tj
T*
(   * Rule 19: Prohibition of felling any green, living tree \(particularly the sacred Khejri tree\).) Tj
T*
(   * Rule 20: Absolute prohibition of killing, hunting, or harming any animal or bird; universal) Tj
T*
(   compassion for all living beings \(Jeev Daya\).) Tj
T*
(   * Hygiene, moral purity, and vegetarianism.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Sacred Ecological Anchor: The Khejri Tree \(Prosopis cineraria\):) Tj
T*
(   The Khejri tree is the life-support tree of the arid Thar Desert: It fixes atmospheric) Tj
T*
(   nitrogen, improves soil moisture and fertility, stabilizes shifting sand dunes, provides green) Tj
T*
(   foliage fodder \(loong\) for livestock during extreme drought, and bears edible protein-rich pods) Tj
T*
(   \(sangri\).) Tj
T*
(   3. The Khejarli Massacre and Martyrdom \(September 1730\):) Tj
T*
(   - Historical Event: Maharaja Abhai Singh of Jodhpur ordered his royal soldiers to fell green) Tj
T*
(   Khejri trees in the Bishnoi village of Khejarli to burn lime for his new royal palace.) Tj
T*
(   - Amrita Devi's Heroic Resistance:) Tj
T*
(   Amrita Devi Bishnoi, a rural village mother, protested that felling green trees violated the) Tj
T*
(   core tenets of their faith. When the royal officers refused to stop, she wrapped her arms) Tj
T*
(   around a marked Khejri tree, proclaiming her immortal words:) Tj
T*
(   'Sir santhe rookh rahe to bhi sasto jaan!') Tj
T*
(   \(Even if one's head is severed to save a tree, the price is small!\)) Tj
T*
(   - The Sacrifice of 363 Bishnois:) Tj
T*
(   The royal axemen severed Amrita Devi's head. Her three young daughters \(Asu, Ratni, and Bhagu\)) Tj
T*
(   stepped forward and were similarly beheaded while hugging the trees. Inspired by their) Tj
T*
(   martyrdom, 363 Bishnoi men and women from 84 surrounding villages sequentially stepped forward,) Tj
T*
(   hugging the trees and sacrificing their lives until the horrified Maharaja halted the) Tj
T*
