12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the four-step Environmental Health Risk Assessment \(EHRA\) framework defined by the US National Research Council \(NRC\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Four-Step Environmental Health Risk Assessment \(EHRA\) Paradigm \(NRC, 1983\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Framework:) Tj
T*
(   Codified in the landmark 1983 NRC 'Red Book' \(Risk Assessment in the Federal Government\), EHRA) Tj
T*
(   is the systematic, quantitative scientific process used to estimate the nature and probability) Tj
T*
(   of adverse human health effects resulting from exposure to environmental chemical pollutants:) Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Sequential Analytical Steps:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Hazard Identification:) Tj
T*
(   * Determining whether exposure to a chemical agent is causally linked to specific adverse) Tj
T*
(   health outcomes \(carcinogenesis, teratogenicity, neurotoxicity, mutagenicity\).) Tj
T*
(   * Synthesizes data from human occupational epidemiological studies, long-term in-vivo rodent) Tj
T*
(   bioassays, in-vitro genotoxicity assays \(Ames Salmonella test\), and Structure-Activity) Tj
T*
(   Relationship \(SAR\) computational modeling.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Dose-Response Assessment:) Tj
T*
(   * Quantifying the mathematical relationship between the dose of a toxicant received \(mg/kg-day\)) Tj
T*
(   and the incidence or severity of adverse biological response:) Tj
T*
(   * Non-Carcinogens: Assumed to exhibit a biological Threshold dose below which homeostatic) Tj
T*
(   cellular repair mechanisms neutralize toxicity. Establishes the Reference Dose \(RfD\) or) Tj
T*
(   Acceptable Daily Intake \(ADI\).) Tj
T*
(   * Carcinogens \(Genotoxic\): Assumed to operate without a threshold \(linear low-dose model: any) Tj
T*
(   non-zero exposure carries a finite theoretical probability of initiating DNA mutation\). Derives) Tj
T*
(   the Cancer Slope Factor \(SF\), representing the 95% upper-bound incremental cancer risk per unit) Tj
T*
(   dose [\(mg/kg-day\)^-1].) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Exposure Assessment:) Tj
T*
(   * Quantifying the magnitude, frequency, duration, and pathways of human contact with the) Tj
T*
(   environmental toxicant:) Tj
T*
(   * Evaluates exposure pathways: Ingestion \(drinking water, food chain\), Inhalation \(ambient) Tj
T*
(   particulates, vapors\), and Dermal Absorption.) Tj
T*
(   * Computes the Chronic Daily Intake \(CDI\):) Tj
T*
(   CDI = \(C * IR * EF * ED\) / \(BW * AT\)) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Risk Characterization:) Tj
T*
(   * Synthesizes exposure assessment with dose-response data to determine quantitative risk:) Tj
T*
(   * Non-Carcinogenic Risk: Expressed as the Hazard Quotient \(HQ = CDI / RfD\). If HQ > 1.0,) Tj
T*
(   exposed populations face unacceptable toxic risk.) Tj
T*
(   * Carcinogenic Risk: Incremental Lifetime Cancer Risk \(LCR = CDI * SF\). Regulatory benchmark:) Tj
T*
(   LCR between 10^-6 \(1 in 1,000,000\) and 10^-4 \(1 in 10,000\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
