(   The oral Reference Dose \(RfD, expressed in mg/kg-day\) is an estimate of a daily oral exposure) Tj
T*
(   to the human population \(including sensitive subgroups such as infants and the elderly\) that is) Tj
T*
(   likely to be without an appreciable risk of deleterious non-carcinogenic health effects during) Tj
T*
(   a lifetime.) Tj
T*
(   2. Determination of Critical Toxicological Endpoints:) Tj
T*
(   Derived from chronic or sub-chronic in-vivo animal bioassays evaluating the most sensitive) Tj
T*
(   critical toxic effect:) Tj
T*
(   - NOAEL \(No-Observed-Adverse-Effect Level\):) Tj
T*
(   The highest experimental dosage administered to test animals at which there is no statistically) Tj
T*
(   or biologically significant increase in the frequency or severity of any adverse toxic effect) Tj
T*
(   compared to the control group.) Tj
T*
(   - LOAEL \(Lowest-Observed-Adverse-Effect Level\):) Tj
T*
(   The lowest experimental dosage tested that produces a statistically significant adverse) Tj
T*
(   biological effect. Used when a clean NOAEL is not identified in the empirical dataset.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mathematical Derivation of RfD via Uncertainty Factors:) Tj
T*
(   RfD = NOAEL / \( UF_total * MF \)) Tj
T*
(   Where UF_total is the product of specific 10-fold Uncertainty \(Safety\) Factors \(UF_1 to UF_5\),) Tj
T*
(   and MF is a Modifying Factor \(0.1 to 10\):) Tj
T*
(   - UF_A \(Interspecies Extrapolation, 10x\): Accounts for the uncertainty of extrapolating) Tj
T*
(   toxicological responses from experimental animals \(rats, mice\) to humans, compensating for) Tj
T*
(   metabolic and physiological differences.) Tj
T*
(   - UF_H \(Intraspecies Human Variability, 10x\): Accounts for the biological variation in) Tj
T*
(   sensitivity among human beings, protecting genetically susceptible individuals, pregnant women,) Tj
T*
(   and infants.) Tj
T*
(   - UF_S \(Sub-chronic to Chronic Extrapolation, 10x\): Applied when deriving a lifetime chronic) Tj
T*
(   RfD from a sub-chronic \(e.g., 90-day\) animal feeding study.) Tj
T*
(   - UF_L \(LOAEL to NOAEL Extrapolation, 10x\): Applied when a NOAEL was not observed in the study) Tj
T*
(   and a LOAEL must be utilized as the baseline point of departure.) Tj
T*
(   - UF_D \(Database Completeness, 3x to 10x\): Applied when the underlying toxicological database) Tj
T*
(   lacks key bioassays \(e.g., missing multi-generational reproductive toxicity studies\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Example Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   If a pesticide demonstrates a chronic rat NOAEL = 10.0 mg/kg-day, applying standard 100-fold) Tj
T*
(   uncertainty \(UF_A * UF_H = 10 * 10 = 100\):) Tj
T*
(   RfD = 10.0 / 100 = 0.10 mg/kg-day.) Tj
T*
