(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the applications of Satellite Remote Sensing in environmental management, detailing multispectral sensors, NDVI, and forest monitoring.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Satellite Remote Sensing: Physical Principles, Sensor Technology, and Environmental Monitoring:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Principles of Electromagnetic Remote Sensing:) Tj
T*
(   Satellite remote sensing measures reflected solar radiation or emitted thermal radiation from) Tj
T*
(   Earth's surface features across specific bands of the electromagnetic \(EM\) spectrum:) Tj
T*
(   - Visible Spectrum \(Blue: 0.45-0.51 um, Green: 0.53-0.59 um, Red: 0.64-0.67 um\).) Tj
T*
(   - Near-Infrared \(NIR, 0.85-0.88 um\): Extremely sensitive to plant internal leaf cellular) Tj
T*
(   structure.) Tj
T*
(   - Shortwave Infrared \(SWIR, 1.57-1.65 um\): Sensitive to vegetation and soil moisture.) Tj
T*
(   - Thermal Infrared \(TIR, 10.4-12.5 um\): Measures surface kinetic brightness temperature.) Tj
T*
(   2. Spectral Reflectance Signatures of Earth Features:) Tj
T*
(   - Green Photosynthetic Vegetation:) Tj
T*
(   * Visible Red Absorption: Chlorophyll-a and -b pigments absorb 80-90% of red light \(0.66 um\) to) Tj
T*
(   drive the light reactions of photosynthesis.) Tj
T*
(   * High NIR Reflectance: The spongy mesophyll cell architecture inside healthy leaves scatters) Tj
T*
(   and reflects over 50-60% of incident Near-Infrared radiation to prevent solar overheating.) Tj
T*
(   - Water Bodies: Highly absorbs both red and NIR wavelengths; clear deep water exhibits) Tj
T*
(   near-zero reflectance in NIR bands.) Tj
T*
(   - Bare Soil / Urban Concrete: Monotonically increasing reflectance from visible to SWIR without) Tj
T*
