T*
(   3. The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index \(NDVI, Rouse et al., 1974\):) Tj
T*
(   NDVI = \(rho_NIR - rho_Red\) / \(rho_NIR + rho_Red\)) Tj
T*
(   - NDVI ranges strictly between -1.0 and +1.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Dense, Healthy Tropical Forest: NDVI = 0.65 to 0.85 \(Massive NIR reflection, near-zero red) Tj
T*
(   reflection\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sparse Grassland / Shrub: NDVI = 0.20 to 0.40.) Tj
T*
(   - Bare Soil / Desert Sand: NDVI = 0.05 to 0.15.) Tj
T*
(   - Water Bodies & Snow: NDVI = Negative values \(-0.1 to -0.6\) because red reflectance exceeds) Tj
T*
(   NIR.) Tj
T*
(   4. Operational Environmental Applications in India:) Tj
T*
(   - Forest Survey of India \(FSI\): Utilizes multi-spectral sensors \(IRS LISS-III, Sentinel-2,) Tj
T*
(   Landsat-8\) to publish the biennial India State of Forest Report \(ISFR\), classifying forest) Tj
T*
(   canopy cover into Very Dense Forest \(> 70% canopy\), Moderately Dense \(40-70%\), and Open Forest) Tj
T*
(   \(10-40%\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tracking Deforestation and Encroachment: Automated digital change-detection algorithms) Tj
T*
(   identify illegal logging and forest fires in real time.) Tj
T*
(   - Disaster Monitoring: Flood inundation mapping during monsoons \(using Synthetic Aperture Radar) Tj
T*
(   SAR from Sentinel-1, which penetrates cloud cover\), tracking Himalayan glacial lake outburst) Tj
T*
(   floods \(GLOFs\), and measuring urban heat island expansion.) Tj
