(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the role of Geographic Information Systems \(GIS\) in environmental decision-making, spatial overlay analysis, and watershed modeling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Geographic Information Systems \(GIS\): Spatial Architecture, Overlay Analysis, and Watershed) Tj
T*
(   Modeling:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Definition of GIS:) Tj
T*
(   A computer-based hardware, software, and geospatial database system designed to capture, store,) Tj
T*
(   manipulate, analyze, model, and display spatially referenced geographical data.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fundamental Data Models:) Tj
T*
(   - Vector Data Model: Represents geographical features as discrete geometric coordinates: Points) Tj
T*
(   \(groundwater tubewells, pollution monitoring stations\), Lines \(rivers, highways, fault lines\),) Tj
T*
(   and Polygons \(national parks, soil textural units, municipal administrative boundaries\), with) Tj
T*
(   associated tabular attribute tables.) Tj
T*
(   - Raster Data Model: Represents continuous spatial phenomena as a regular grid of square cells) Tj
T*
(   \(pixels\), where each cell has a specific coordinate and numerical value \(e.g., Digital) Tj
T*
(   Elevation Models DEM, satellite NDVI imagery, precipitation grids\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Geospatial Analytical Operations:) Tj
T*
(   - Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis \(MCDA\) & Weighted Overlay:) Tj
T*
(   * Used for industrial site selection, landfill siting, or critical tiger corridor design.) Tj
T*
(   * Re-classifying and weighting multiple thematic data layers \(Slope, Distance to River, Soil) Tj
T*
(   Permeability, Depth to Water Table, Distance to Settlement\).) Tj
T*
(   * Siting a Sanitary Landfill: Overlaying layers with Boolean constraints \(Slope < 5%, Distance) Tj
T*
(   to river > 500 m, Clay content > 40%, Distance to highway > 1 km\) to identify optimal) Tj
T*
(   environmentally compliant land parcels.) Tj
T*
(   - Buffer Generation: Generating automated proximity zones \(e.g., 500-meter buffer around rivers) Tj
T*
(   to establish no-construction zones\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Hydrological Watershed Modeling \(ArcSWAT / HEC-HMS Integration\):) Tj
T*
(   - Derives watershed flow direction and flow accumulation grids from high-resolution satellite) Tj
T*
(   DEMs \(SRTM, Cartosat\).) Tj
T*
(   - Delineates micro-watershed boundaries, stream drainage networks, and computes) Tj
T*
(   time-of-concentration \(T_c\) for runoff.) Tj
T*
