(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the role of Environmental Education in India, analyzing the Supreme Court directives in the M.C. Mehta litigation and Eco-Club programs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Environmental Education in India: Judicial Directives, Pedagogical Integration, and Eco-Clubs:) Tj
T*
(   1. Constitutional and Judicial Genesis:) Tj
T*
(   Environmental education is recognized in Indian jurisprudence not merely as an academic) Tj
T*
(   pursuit, but as a constitutional imperative essential to give practical effect to the) Tj
T*
(   Fundamental Duty under Article 51A\(g\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Historic Supreme Court Directives \(M.C. Mehta v. Union of India, 1991\):) Tj
T*
(   Environmental public interest attorney M.C. Mehta filed a landmark writ petition seeking court) Tj
T*
(   orders to educate citizens regarding environmental preservation.) Tj
T*
(   - In its historic December 1991 ruling, the Supreme Court of India issued sweeping nationwide) Tj
T*
(   mandatory directives:) Tj
T*
(   * 1. Broadcast Media Mandate: Directed all national and state television and radio networks) Tj
T*
(   \(Doordarshan, All India Radio\) to broadcast daily educational environmental public service) Tj
T*
(   programs and short cinema slides free of cost.) Tj
T*
(   * 2. Compulsory Curricular Mandate: Ordered that environmental education must be made a) Tj
T*
(   COMPULSORY subject in all educational institutions across India, from primary schools through) Tj
T*
(   colleges and universities.) Tj
T*
(   * 3. Implementation Directive: Directed state governments, education boards \(NCERT, CBSE, UGC\),) Tj
T*
(   and universities to formulate standardized compulsory core environmental science syllabi for) Tj
T*
(   all undergraduate bachelor's degree programs \(Engineering, Medicine, Arts, Science, Commerce\).) Tj
T*
(   3. The National Green Corps \(NGC\) 'Eco-Clubs' Program:) Tj
T*
(   - Launched in 2001 by the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change.) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Established across more than 100,000 schools and colleges nationwide, managed) Tj
T*
(   by State Nodal Agencies.) Tj
T*
(   - Student Participatory Activities:) Tj
T*
(   * Establishing biodiversity gardens and medicinal plant nurseries on school campuses.) Tj
T*
(   * Conducting localized energy audits and school plastic waste segregation campaigns.) Tj
T*
(   * Water quality testing of community tubewells using low-cost field test kits.) Tj
T*
(   * Organizing annual public awareness rallies celebrating World Environment Day \(June 5\), Earth) Tj
T*
(   Day \(April 22\), and Wildlife Week.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
