(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the socio-economic and cultural impacts of Development-Induced Displacement, evaluating the marginalization of Project-Affected Persons \(PAPs\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Development-Induced Displacement: Socio-Economic Impacts and Marginalization of PAPs:) Tj
T*
(   1. Magnitude of Development Displacement in India:) Tj
T*
(   Since independence in 1947, large-scale infrastructural developmental projects \(multipurpose) Tj
T*
(   hydroelectric dams, open-cast coal mines, steel plants, expressways, industrial special) Tj
T*
(   economic zones\) have displaced an estimated 50 to 60 million Project-Affected Persons \(PAPs\) in) Tj
T*
(   India.) Tj
T*
(   - Disproportionate Adivasi Burden: Although indigenous Scheduled Tribes \(Adivasis\) comprise) Tj
T*
(   only ~8.6% of India's national population, they represent over 40% to 50% of all displaced) Tj
T*
(   persons, because mineral wealth and dam catchments overlap predominantly with ancestral tribal) Tj
T*
(   forest homelands.) Tj
T*
(   2. Multi-Dimensional Socioeconomic Pathology: Michael Cernea's Impoverishment Risks Model) Tj
T*
(   \(IRR\):) Tj
T*
(   Anthropologist Michael Cernea identified eight interconnected, systemic impoverishment) Tj
T*
(   processes that afflict displaced populations in the absence of comprehensive rehabilitation:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Landlessness: Expropriation of agricultural land severs the primary productive economic) Tj
T*
(   asset of rural agrarian households. Cash compensation is rapidly depleted on immediate) Tj
T*
(   consumption.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Joblessness: Loss of agricultural wage labor and rural artisanal employment; agrarian) Tj
T*
(   farmers lack technical industrial skills to secure permanent employment in modern mechanized) Tj
T*
(   factories.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Homelessness: Loss of physical shelter; displaced families languish in temporary tin) Tj
T*
(   shacks in informal squatter settlements for years.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Marginalization: Downward socioeconomic mobility, chronic debt bondage to private) Tj
T*
(   moneylenders, and loss of human dignity.) Tj
T*
(   - 5. Food Insecurity: Caloric and protein malnutrition surges, increasing infant mortality and) Tj
T*
(   stunting.) Tj
T*
(   - 6. Increased Morbidity and Mortality: Stress-induced cardiovascular illness, water-borne) Tj
T*
(   epidemics in unhygienic resettlement colonies.) Tj
T*
