(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the statutory framework of the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 \(LARR Act\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The LARR Act, 2013: Statutory Architecture, Consent Clauses, and Mandatory Rehabilitation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Legislative Replacement of Colonial Law:) Tj
T*
(   Enacted in 2013, the LARR Act repealed and replaced the archaic colonial Land Acquisition Act) Tj
T*
(   of 1894, which permitted involuntary state expropriation under the autocratic doctrine of) Tj
T*
(   Eminent Domain with meager cash compensation and zero legal entitlement to rehabilitation.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mandatory Social Impact Assessment \(SIA, Chapter II\):) Tj
T*
(   - An independent SIA study must be conducted in consultation with local Panchayats/Gram Sabhas) Tj
T*
(   before initiating any land acquisition.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluates: Whether the proposed acquisition serves a genuine public purpose, the exact number) Tj
T*
(   of affected families, the impact on public utilities and common property resources, and) Tj
T*
(   assesses whether alternative non-agricultural or degraded land could be utilized.) Tj
T*
(   - SIA report is reviewed by an independent multi-disciplinary Expert Group; if the social costs) Tj
T*
(   outweigh the public benefits, the acquisition can be halted.) Tj
T*
(   3. Stringent Consent Thresholds \(Section 2\(2\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Where land is acquired for private corporate companies or public-private partnerships \(PPP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Prior informed written consent of at least 80% of affected land-owning families is legally) Tj
T*
(   mandatory for acquisitions on behalf of private companies.) Tj
T*
(   - Prior consent of at least 70% of affected families is mandatory for Public-Private) Tj
T*
(   Partnership \(PPP\) projects.) Tj
T*
(   - In Scheduled Areas \(tribal belts under Fifth Schedule\): Mandatory prior informed consent of) Tj
T*
(   the local Gram Sabha under PESA 1996.) Tj
T*
(   4. Comprehensive Financial Compensation Package:) Tj
T*
(   - Rural Areas: Assessed baseline market value is multiplied by a rural factor \(up to 2.0\). A) Tj
T*
(   100% Solatium \(statutory compensation for involuntary acquisition\) is added on top, ensuring) Tj
T*
(   total financial compensation equals up to FOUR TIMES \(4x\) the base market value!) Tj
T*
(   - Urban Areas: Total compensation equals TWO TIMES \(2x\) the market value.) Tj
T*
(   5. Mandatory Resettlement and Rehabilitation \(R&R, Second and Third Schedules\):) Tj
T*
(   The Act legally decouples land acquisition from mere cash: every displaced family is) Tj
T*
(   statutorily entitled to:) Tj
T*
(   - A constructed permanent housing unit \(not less than 50 m2 plinth area in rural areas\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mandatory employment for at least one member per affected family, or a one-time cash) Tj
T*
(   financial assistance of 5 lakh rupees.) Tj
T*
(   - An ongoing monthly subsistence allowance \(3,000 rupees/month for one year\).) Tj
T*
(   - 25 infrastructural amenities in the resettlement colony \(schools, primary health centers,) Tj
T*
(   piped water, electricity, community halls, playgrounds\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
