(   model\) to predict steady-state downwind pollutant concentrations from an elevated continuous) Tj
T*
(   point source \(chimney stack\):) Tj
T*
(   - Assumptions: Continuous steady emission rate Q \(g/s\); uniform horizontal wind velocity u) Tj
T*
(   \(m/s\); complete ground reflection \(no surface deposition\); steady meteorological stability;) Tj
T*
(   pollutant behaves as an inert, non-reactive gas; crosswind and vertical concentration profiles) Tj
T*
(   follow normal \(Gaussian\) bell-shaped distributions.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   The pollutant concentration C\(x,y,z\) at downwind distance x, crosswind distance y, and vertical) Tj
T*
(   receptor height z above ground is given by:) Tj
T*
(   C\(x,y,z\) = [ Q / \(2 * pi * u * sigma_y * sigma_z\) ] * exp[ -0.5 * \(y / sigma_y\)^2 ] * { exp[) Tj
T*
(   -0.5 * \(\(z - H\) / sigma_z\)^2 ] + exp[ -0.5 * \(\(z + H\) / sigma_z\)^2 ] }) Tj
T*
(   Where:) Tj
T*
(   - Q: Pollutant mass emission rate \(g/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - u: Mean wind speed at effective stack release height \(m/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - H: Effective stack release height \(m\), equal to physical stack height \(h_s\) plus) Tj
T*
(   buoyant/momentum plume rise \(Delta h\).) Tj
T*
(   - sigma_y: Horizontal crosswind dispersion coefficient \(m\).) Tj
T*
(   - sigma_z: Vertical dispersion coefficient \(m\).) Tj
T*
(   Both sigma_y and sigma_z expand continuously as power functions of downwind distance x.) Tj
T*
(   - The second exponential bracket accounts for the 'virtual source' at -H representing 100%) Tj
T*
(   upward reflection of the plume off the ground surface.) Tj
T*
(   - Ground-Level Plume Centerline Concentration \(y = 0, z = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   C\(x,0,0\) = [ Q / \(pi * u * sigma_y * sigma_z\) ] * exp[ -0.5 * \(H / sigma_z\)^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Pasquill-Gifford Atmospheric Stability Classes:) Tj
T*
(   Atmospheric turbulence and vertical temperature gradients are categorized into six stability) Tj
T*
(   classes \(A to F\) based on surface wind speed and incoming solar insolation \(day\) or cloud cover) Tj
T*
(   \(night\):) Tj
T*
(   - Class A: Extremely Unstable \(strong solar insolation, light winds, vigorous thermal) Tj
T*
(   convection\).) Tj
T*
(   - Class B: Moderately Unstable.) Tj
T*
(   - Class C: Slightly Unstable.) Tj
T*
(   - Class D: Neutral \(overcast day or night, high winds > 6 m/s; mechanical shear turbulence) Tj
T*
(   dominates\).) Tj
T*
(   - Class E: Slightly Stable \(nighttime, moderate radiative cooling\).) Tj
T*
(   - Class F: Moderately Stable \(clear nighttime, light winds < 2 m/s, strong radiation) Tj
T*
(   temperature inversion, near-zero vertical mixing, trapping chimney smoke near ground in) Tj
T*
(   dangerous 'Fumigation' plumes\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
