/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the engineering principles of Circular Sustainable Cities, evaluating the Kalundborg Industrial Symbiosis paradigm and Urban Metabolism.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Circular Sustainable Cities: Urban Metabolism and the Kalundborg Industrial Symbiosis Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Concept of Urban Metabolism \(Abel Wolman, 1965\):) Tj
T*
(   - Linear Urban Metabolism \(Unsustainable\): A modern consumer city functions as an open,) Tj
T*
(   throughput linear system: vast quantities of raw virgin resources \(fossil energy, food,) Tj
T*
(   freshwater, construction sand\) are sucked in from distant hinterlands, metabolized) Tj
T*
(   inefficiently, and discharged as concentrated, unassimilated waste outputs \(greenhouse gases,) Tj
T*
(   toxic sewage, landfill garbage\).) Tj
T*
(   - Circular Urban Metabolism \(Sustainable\): Re-engineers urban resource flows to mimic natural) Tj
T*
(   ecological nutrient cycles: waste streams from one urban subsystem are systematically captured,) Tj
T*
(   purified, and redirected as secondary input feedstocks for another subsystem, minimizing net) Tj
T*
(   external resource inputs and eliminating waste emissions.) Tj
T*
